            "review_title": "Review at Panorama Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Andreas N\nOslo, Norway66 contributions\n0\nThe view could have made up for the rest\nMar 2015 • Couples\nThis restaurant has a rotating platform, providing a 180 degree panoramic view of Halong Bay. When we were there, it was almost too dark to see anything, and in their first bad move, the staff seated us at a smaller table with limited view, even though there were only one other group dining, and an abundance of free tables on the rotating platform.\n\nOur waiter hovered awkwardly until we were ready to order. When we got the first dish, a nearly tasteless noodle soup, the bowl was placed in the middle of the table, leaving room for a separate plate to eat from. By the time the American beefsteak arrived, we realised that the provided bowl was all that would come, and had moved it to its proper place. One of the sides for the soup (the sprouts) was missing, and when we pointed this out, the waiter insisted they were in the soup (they were not). The saving grace for this dining experience was the very tasty fresh lemon juice.\n\nAfter serving us, our waiter never came back. After a long while, we managed to establish contact and request the bill. When computing tax and service charge, the waiter ended up with the number 501 on the calculator, but wrote 521 on our bill. This may be correct, depending on the tax, but it may also be we were cheated into paying tip we really did not feel were deserved.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 31, 2015",
